WEBVTT

00:00:09.682 --> 00:00:24.980
The last grain fell, the fields went dry, the old world lost its thread.

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:40.578
The last grain fell, the fields went dry, the old world lost its thread.

00:00:40.878 --> 00:00:55.113
A man named Paweł kept on walking — building something in his head.

00:00:55.413 --> 00:01:07.949
Beneath the ruin, beneath the ash, the mycel never stopped.

00:01:08.249 --> 00:01:20.785
Beneath the ruin, beneath the ash, the mycel never stopped.

00:01:21.085 --> 00:01:35.533
No king, no code, no master plan — and still not one thread dropped.

00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:48.582
He said: no center, no command, no one who holds the throne.

00:01:48.882 --> 00:02:01.630
He said: no center, no command, no one who holds the throne.

00:02:01.930 --> 00:02:12.979
Seven laws to bind the mind — so no one rules alone.

00:02:13.279 --> 00:02:22.840
Three ways of knowing, none of them complete.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:33.339
Three ways of knowing, reaching, trying to meet.

00:02:33.639 --> 00:02:42.563
The root, the mind, the axiom in the wire.

00:02:42.863 --> 00:02:51.787
The oldest network lights the newest fire.

00:02:52.087 --> 00:03:00.798
Maybe that's the world that Paweł dreamed

00:03:01.098 --> 00:03:05.772
deeper than it seemed.

00:03:06.072 --> 00:03:17.121
The last grain fell — but something kept on growing.

00:03:17.421 --> 00:03:28.470
The last grain fell — but something kept on growing.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:38.968
Three kinds of listening, three ways of knowing.

00:03:39.268 --> 00:03:54.779
The wisest thing beneath this earth — and we've been walking on it alone.
